+ row  `F32`  `float`, `unrestricted float`
+ row  `F64`  `double`, `unrestricted double`
+ row  `List[T]`  `sequence<T>`, `FrozenArray<T>`
+ row  `Map[K, V]`  `record<K, V>`
+ row  `Optional[T]`  `T?`, avec `Unset` pour `null`

= row  `Optional[T]`  `T?`, with `Unset` as `null`
- ```
+ ```

- The numbers are [sized](numbers.md#numeric-types), so a parameter which is declared `long`
- takes an `S32`, and not an unsized `Int`:
+ Les nombres ont une [taille](numbers.md#numeric-types) ; un paramètre déclaré `long` prend
+ donc un `S32`, et non un `Int` sans taille :

= takes an `S32`, and not an unsized `Int`:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val left: S32 = 0
+ val left: S32 = 0

- val top: S32 = 480
+ val top: S32 = 480

- val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)
+ val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)

= val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)
- ```
+ ```

- Each argument is checked against the declared type of its parameter, in the foreign type
- system's own terms. `scrollTo` wants two values of the foreign type `s32`, and an `S32` is
- the Scala value which provides one.
+ Chaque argument est vérifié par rapport au type déclaré de son paramètre, dans les termes
+ propres au système de types étranger. `scrollTo` attend deux valeurs du type étranger `s32`,
+ et un `S32` est la valeur Scala qui en fournit une.

- ### Serializing to JavaScript
+ ### Sérialiser en JavaScript

- A foreign value's `expr` is its expression, a `Foreign.Expression`, which is a small tree of
- these nodes:
+ L'`expr` d'une valeur étrangère est son expression, une `Foreign.Expression`, qui est un
+ petit arbre composé de ces nœuds :

= these nodes:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Node
- column  Stands for
- column  Renders as
- row  `Reference(name)`  a global  `document`
- row  `Select(target, member, owner)`  a member of a value  `target.member`
- row  `Apply(target, arguments)`  a call  `target(arguments)`
- row  `Index(target, index)`  an index access  `target[index]`
- row  `Literal(value)`  a constant  `'text'`, `42`
+ column  Nœud
+ column  Représente
+ column  Se rend en
+ row  `Reference(name)`  une globale  `document`
+ row  `Select(target, member, owner)`  un membre d'une valeur  `target.member`
+ row  `Apply(target, arguments)`  un appel  `target(arguments)`
+ row  `Index(target, index)`  un accès indexé  `target[index]`
+ row  `Literal(value)`  une constante  `'text'`, `42`

= row  `Literal(value)`  a constant  `'text'`, `42`
- ```
+ ```

- `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
+ `Javascript.serialize` écrit l'arbre sous forme de code source JavaScript :

= `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
